ate on the complete S1-S6 behavioral suite set plus whole-tree fingerprint/outcome comparison.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a Plan/Outcome step describing the bounded provider, AWS review-bot/op-cert, and reconciler check/dry-run/live canary drills that AC4 attests to, so the operator-attested criterion maps to described work.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T2","T4"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.28,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC4: 'Bounded provider, AWS review-bot/op-cert, and reconciler check/dry-run/live canaries pass with required redacted evidence...'","Plan steps 1-3 enumerate subsystem cutover, draining, and comparison recording but never mention provider/AWS/reconciler canaries","Outcome section only references 'provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged'"],"finding":"AC4 introduces a substantial operator-attested deliverable — 'Bounded provider, AWS review-bot/op-cert, and reconciler check/dry-run/live canaries' with redacted evidence — that is not described anywhere in the Context, Outcome, or Plan sections. The plan body only mentions 'provider-neutral outcomes' generally, giving AC4 no covering description.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f63bf9047cce6c43e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, 4th bullet ([operator-attested])","norm_id":"n7faa6bcb39ec58f9","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor reads the Plan, cuts reads to seams, drains the gate, and never runs the canary drills because no step describes them"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a Plan bullet: e.g. '4. Run the bounded provider + AWS review-bot/op-cert + reconciler check/dry-run/live canaries; capture redacted run/change ids, selected provider/auth-source kind, retry/cache counters, fingerprint/outcome, and rollback decision as the operator attestation.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add child ACs covering removal of migration switches, per-job ambient reloads, and migration exceptions, plus documenting the retained S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC3: 'Legacy facades, switches, per-job ambient reloads, and migration exceptions are removed only after their proof passes; documented rollback retains the S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor.'","Every child's rollback reads identically: 'No stored ticket/event/binding format changes. A legacy facade is removed only after its focused suite passes; until then rollback selects the facade.' — no mention of migration switches, per-job ambient reloads, migration exceptions, or the S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor.","container pairing: parent + 1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4/6633-219e-988a-42f6/9515-ffa1-5272-4310/9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8/d074-ab22-e37a-4480/ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36"],"finding":"Parent AC3's specific sub-clauses — removal of migration switches, per-job ambient reloads, and migration exceptions, AND the documented rollback retaining the 'S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor' — are not delivered by any child; children's rollback prose only covers generic 'legacy facade removed after focused suite passes.'","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f796f4e0a05ad7feb","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"child ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36 and all siblings (Compatibility/rollback sections)","norm_id":"n34283a1eddd38dfc","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A per-job ambient reload or migration switch survives because no child names it for removal; the parent's compatibility-floor documentation requirement is never produced."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Extend the terminal slice ed65 to explicitly assert removal of the non-facade legacy constructs and to produce the documented S1-compatibility-floor rollback note.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary"