0 (no ordering edge)","scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py: 9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8 & d074-ab22-e37a-4480 (no ordering edge)"],"finding":"Sibling tickets touch the same file(s) with no ordering edge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82524518cbf636a6","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"na0177dc3af65d74f","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a depends_on/blocks edge to serialize, or partition the file ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[operator-attested] Bounded provider, AWS review-bot/op-cert, and reconciler che' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly that after the MCP config-read cutover the write/live/LLM authorization gates (_readonly, _mcp_gate) retain their fail-CLOSED direction on malformed/absent config under the new startup/snapshot binding, and add a targeted test asserting the fail-closed default is preserved (not just generic fingerprint equality).","cohort":["T5c"],"criteria":["T5c"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5562,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'per-job ambient reloads ... are removed' and 'mcp_server load_config()-per-call cutover deferred from RP-04 S5'","Repo: src/rebar/mcp_server.py:415-424 _mcp_gate resolves REBAR_MCP_<ATTR> via load_config() per call and returns `fail` (fail-closed) on ConfigError; _readonly() is 'Fail-CLOSED (read-only) on a malformed config'","Existing sound contract in _mcp_auth.py (fail-closed startup gate, RFC 8707 audience re-check, redaction) means this is ADVISORY/minor, not a new-surface HIGH"],"finding":"The plan reroutes the read path of the boundary-crossing MCP authorization gates (_readonly / _mcp_gate for REBAR_MCP_READONLY, REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_JIRA_SYNC, REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM) from per-call load_config() reads (currently fail-CLOSED on malformed config, mcp_server.py:415-424) to a startup/snapshot binding and removes 'per-job ambient reloads', but only asserts generic fingerprint/outcome equality — it does not explicitly assert that these security gates retain their fail-closed direction under the new binding.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f822f9292a213af28","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 (mcp_server/_mcp_auth cutover); Testing bullet; AC4","norm_id":"n1a0a48b828d59ce6","priority":0.3438,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A malformed/absent config after startup binding could resolve an MCP write/live/LLM gate to the permissive direction if the snapshot seam does not preserve the per-gate fail-closed default that the per-call resolver enforced."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the Testing section, add a fail-closed regression check for the MCP authorization gates: assert that a malformed config resolves REBAR_MCP_READONLY-gated writes and REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_JIRA_SYNC/ALLOW_LLM to the safe (hidden/denied) direction under the snapshot seam, matching the current _mcp_gate `fail` behavior.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a whole-tree AC (in ed65 or parent) asserting the ownership gate enforces exactly one owner per declared config/credential name.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.675,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC1: '…every declared config/credential name has one owner; the legacy exception set is EMPTY; no exception uses a path glob.'","Child ACs assert 'cut-to-seam or registered as an owned (non-legacy) entry with rationale' and 'no path-glob exception' but none asserts each declared name resolves to exactly ONE owner.","container pairing: parent + 1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4/6633-219e-988a-42f6/9515-ffa1-5272-4310/9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8/d074-ab22-e37a-4480/ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36"],"finding":"Parent AC1's 'every declared config/credential name has one owner' (single-owner uniqueness property) is not asserted by any child; children assert absence of below-seam reads and per-file registration but not name->single-owner uniqueness across the tree (partial-without-remainder).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f70904c00ab374909","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"child ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36 and all siblings","norm_id":"n4b5e02d7ce8a868c","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two owners register the same config/credential name across different subsystems; no child's held-out test detects the duplicate-owner condition."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Have ed65's held-out or the gate assert single-owner uniqueness across the drained tree.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a one-line positive rationale for the per-subsystem cut/prove/remove unit (why each subsystem's facade is removed only after ITS focused suite passes — blast-radius containment and isolated rollback), so the sequencing property is explicit rather than implied.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3643,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 2: 'Drain the legacy-exception set to empty; remove legacy facades/switches only after each subsystem's suite passes.'","Compatibility: 'Do not remove a legacy facade until its focused suite and bounded path pass; before removal, rollback selects the facade.' — a constraint, not a stated positive rationale for the per-subsystem unit.","ADR 0098 supplies the architectural rationale; the local sequencing-unit choice is this slice's own and is unjustified in the plan text."],"finding":"The plan executes an already-accepted architecture (ADR 0098) but does not state a positive rationale for its one genuine local design choice: performing the cut/prove/remove at per-subsystem granularity (reconciler engine; store/snapshot/io; cli/commands; llm/workflow; mcp_server) rather than cutting all reads then removing all facades. The Compatibility section states the sequencing rule ('do not remove a facade until its focused suite and bounded path pass') but never affirmatively says why the subsystem is the chosen unit (e.g. blast-radius containment / granular rollback).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa20fb9193eb7c392","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1-2 and Compatibility / rollback","norm_id":"n18a1c68582a61325","priority":0.2357,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer could reasonably batch the cutover differently (e.g. all reads, then all facades) and lose the granular rollback the plan implicitly relies on."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In the Compatibility/rollback section add: 'Subsystem-by-subsystem is the cutover unit because it bounds blast radius and keeps each facade's rollback isolated to its own focused suite; a facade is removed only once its subsystem's oracle is green, so a regression rolls back one subsystem, not the whole slice.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Declare an explicit ordering/dependency making ed65 (S7.3.f) run after slices a-e, so its whole-tree-EMPTY assertion is well-founded.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ed65 Context: 'This is the LAST subsystem slice: after it, the whole-tree LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS list … reaches EMPTY. This slice asserts that end state…'","ed65's held-out asserts check() returns no finding containing its listed paths AND its entries removed — but the 'whole-tree EMPTY' end-state claim depends on a-e; no ordering/dependency edge is stated in any child.","Parent plan step 2: 'remove legacy facades/switches only after each subsystem's suite passes' implies serialization but children carry no explicit sequence.","container pairing: parent + 1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4/6633-219e-988a-42f6/9515-ffa1-5272-4310/9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8/d074-ab22-e37a-4480/ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36"],"finding":"Ordering violation / dependency gap: child ed65 (S7.3.f) asserts the WHOLE-TREE LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS reaches EMPTY and 'asserts that end state', which requires all five sibling slices (a-e) to have drained their entries first, but no child declares a depends_on/ordering edge sequencing ed65 last.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5c98e40d08e89e3d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36","norm_id":"ndaac716f4b26b8fe","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["ed65 is executed/merged before one of a-e has drained; the whole-tree-EMPTY assertion (parent AC1 end state) is falsely satisfied or ed65's terminal claim fails intermittently."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add depends_on edges from ed65 to 1b07/6633/9515/9e42/d074, or restate the whole-tree-EMPTY assertion as gated on all sibling held-outs.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_